/* =========================================================================
   BIBLE-DATA-TEMPLATE.JS
   =========================================================================
   Hardcoded with three public-domain versions: World English Bible (WEB),
   King James Version (KJV), and American Standard Version (ASV).
   Source: BibleHub PDF exports, parsed into this app's data format.

   This file defines one global object: BIBLE_DATA

   ---------------------------------------------------------------------
   ADDING MORE VERSIONS
   ---------------------------------------------------------------------
   Add a new entry to "versions" below, then add that version's id as a
   key inside any verse's "text" object, e.g.:

     text: { web: "...", kjv: "...", asv: "...", niv: "..." }

   Note: only public-domain translations (like WEB, KJV, ASV, Young's
   Literal Translation, Darby, etc.) can be added this way. Actively
   copyrighted translations (NIV, ESV, NASB, NKJV...) can't have their
   full text reproduced here.

   ---------------------------------------------------------------------
   TITLES (section headings)
   ---------------------------------------------------------------------
   Each chapter may have a "sections" array that inserts a heading
   before a given verse:

     sections: [ { beforeVerse: 4, title: "The Woman at the Well" } ]

   Some sections also carry an optional "reference" field (the italic
   cross-reference line, e.g. "John 1:1-5; Hebrews 11:1-3") that the
   app does not render yet but is kept here for future use. Section
   titles/references are shared across all versions (as in the source).

   ---------------------------------------------------------------------
   FOOTNOTES
   ---------------------------------------------------------------------
   None of the source PDFs used to build this file included footnotes,
   so none are present. To attach a footnote to a word, insert a
   {{fn:marker}} token after the word in the verse text and add a
   matching entry to that verse's "footnotes" array - see README.md
   for the full syntax.
   ========================================================================= */

